            <ArticleTitle>[Right-sided hemihepatectomy in echinococcosis of the liver in pregnancy].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>580-2; discussion 582-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The treatment of symptomatic echinococcal disease of the liver during pregnancy is a rare, but difficult problem. A 42 year old, pregnant woman with obstructive jaundice and acute cholangitis due to extensive echinococcus cysticus infection of the right hepatic lobe is presented. A formal, right hemihepatectomy was successfully performed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
